// sensor_die.sbv — Wave 2 C0 substrate fixture: the file IS the die.
//
// Layer 0 (bridge design record): a `.sbv` file's file-scope bare `let`s
// ARE the boundary pins. Pin-ness lives in the TYPE (pin classes are
// valueless markers, std/electronics.bv); direction lives in the class
// (In/Out/Io/IoOd) — no `port` keyword, no declaration-time direction
// (a wire is bidirectional; the current driver decides).
//
// The C1 projection turns exactly these fields into an `.ebv` component:
// pin names = field names, class = field type, arrays element-wise.
// (No explicit import: the `.sbv` prelude provides std/electronics.bv,
// same parity as `.ebv` files — and this exercises the prelude's
// state-anchored fallback.)

let sda: IoOd;
let scl: Out;
let gpio: Io[8];
let vdd: Power;
let gnd: Ground;
